{
  "unit": {
    "id": "6",
    "title": "To, from, through",
    "blurb": "ad, in, ex, per, trans, prope + the right case",
    "intro": "Prepositions decide the case. _in_ with the ablative means 'in', but _in_ with the accusative means 'into': _in hortō_ (in the garden) vs _in hortum_ (into the garden). _ad_ (to) and _per_ (through), _trans_ (across) and _prope_ (near) take the accusative; _ex_ (out of) takes the ablative. When you meet a new preposition, learn it together with its case."
  },
